_LOFI_NOISE_DISPOSITION = "WARN"


def rt60_in_band(noise_disposition: str | None) -> bool:
    """Does the RT60 stage run for a room that measured this noise disposition?

    ONE HOME for the conditional-stage decision (Rick, ruled 2026-08-10): RT60 fires only
    at SNR >= 48 dBA. Below that line the audio is capped at lo-fi and the stage is
    bypassed entirely — so RT60 is genuinely ABSENT for those contributors rather than
    present-but-unmeasured, and no layer needs to learn a special value.

    Every caller that asks "does this contributor have an RT60 axis" routes through here:
    the baseline resolver, both drift gates, the clap endpoints, and the FE stage list.
    That is deliberate. The previous design taught five separate layers the same
    exception and each one that hadn't learned it yet was a defect.

    REJECT is not special-cased: a REJECT noise stage fails its own gate and never
    reaches a clap stage or a baseline, so it cannot arrive here in practice. If it ever
    did, treating it as "RT60 runs" is the safe direction — it keeps an axis rather than
    silently dropping one.
    """
    return (noise_disposition or "").upper() != _LOFI_NOISE_DISPOSITION
